meta {
  name: cancel-order-item
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/admin/v1/orders/{{order_uid}}/items/REPLACE_ITEM_UID/cancel
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "reason": "kitchen ran out"
  }
}

tests {
  test("rejects the placeholder item uid", function () {
    // 404 is expected as written: REPLACE_ITEM_UID is not a real uid. Replace it with an
    // items[].uid from get-order to exercise the real path.
    expect(res.status).to.equal(404)
  })
}

docs {
  # Cancel one line

Replace `REPLACE_ITEM_UID` with an `items[].uid` from `get-order` -- it is left literal on purpose,
because which line to void is a human decision rather than something to chain automatically.

The order is **re-priced** from the remaining active lines in the same transaction. The line is
struck through rather than deleted, so the kitchen ticket history stays intact.

Cancelling the *last* remaining line is refused: an order with no items and a non-zero total is
incoherent, and "cancel the order" is the action actually wanted.
}
